# Implementation Plan: Block Hardness & Tool Types

This plan outlines the changes needed to set custom breaking times (hardness) and the specific tool required to harvest blocks.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] com.modmaker.BlockData
We will update the data class to store the new properties alongside the block name and texture:
- `String miningTool` (values: "Hand", "Pickaxe", "Axe", "Shovel", "Hoe", "Sword")
- `float breakingTime` (The `hardness` of the block in Minecraft logic, e.g., 1.5 for stone, 50.0 for obsidian).

### [MODIFY] com.modmaker.ModMakerApp.java (GUI)
- Inside the "Add Block" section, I will add a dropdown menu (`JComboBox`) containing the tool list.
- I will add a number spinner (`JSpinner`) or text field for the Breaking Time so you can set exactly how long it takes to break.
- The `Add Block` logic will read these fields and pack them into the `BlockData` object.

### [MODIFY] com.modmaker.ModGenerator.java
- **Java Registration Update**: The block's `BlockBehaviour.Properties` will be updated to apply `.destroyTime(value)`. If a tool other than "Hand" or "Sword" is selected, the `.requiresCorrectToolForDrops()` flag will be appended.
- **Data Tags Injection**: In Minecraft 1.20+, tools requirements are controlled strictly via JSON tags. The generator will create new JSON files inside the `src/main/resources/data/minecraft/tags/blocks/mineable/` directory corresponding to the chosen tool (e.g., `pickaxe.json`, `axe.json`). It will group all queued blocks by their tool requirement and list their IDs correctly in these tag lists so that they drop correctly inside the game.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> Are you okay with the default "mining tier" for the tools being regular (like a Wooden/Gold tier requirement)? In standard Minecraft 1.20.1, you only need to specify a tool type tag to make it breakable by any tier of that tool. If you don't explicitly want me to add an *Iron/Diamond* tier tag selector, I'll keep it simple and just bind it to the tool type in general. Let me know if that works!
